  "gain_is_hypothesis_2026_11_19": "UNSETTLED: 'gain_is' (sensible, before the latent multiplier) was the operator's assumption, not read from the standard. Measured: F280-1's sensible 5652 W x 1.3 (Cl. 6.3.1's LM, 'in most applications a multiplier of 1.3') = 7348 W vs 7321 (100.4 %); x 1.3 the 8.3.8 turns read 0.94-0.96 of Annex J, 8.3.7 b 0.95, 8.3.4 c 0.975 (8.3.6 b 1.21). Annex J's gain may be CSCn = LM x sum of HGsr. The 8.3.9 a) page's column header (p. 177+) settles it. The 8.3.9 a) header says only 'Gain, W', and Cl. 8.4.1 'heat gain value(s)': not settled by Annex J; Annex K's base-case room table (p. 184+) may show whether its room gains are HGsr (sensible) and how they total.",
